 "naming_decision": "SPARSE_PANEL_16384 and HEAVY_PANEL_16384 (task table: 'support = their own TRAIN examples; VALIDATION = the M02 definition') are built and registered as two physical manifests each, suffixed _SUPPORT / _VALIDATION exactly like UNEW_VAL / UNEW_TEST; TRUE_COLD_VALIDATION is eval-only (M03 shape, no TRAIN counterpart, cold users have zero eligible TRAIN examples); COLD_H_16384 and WARM_TRUNCATION_16384 are single panel manifests (M04 / M04W shape). DEVIATION: the task packet names this band's physical manifests UNEW_TEST_SUPPORT_32768 / UNEW_TEST_VALIDATION_32768, but v4data.manifests.refuse_test_manifest (LOCKED, not edited) refuses any manifest id containing the substring 'TEST' unconditionally, as a blunt defense-in-depth gate against ever building a TEST-split manifest before ALL_METHODS_LOCK - it would refuse these files outright. The physical manifest ids are therefore UNEW_HOLDOUT_SUPPORT_32768 / UNEW_HOLDOUT_VALIDATION_32768. The registry role key was first kept as the task's own 'UNSEEN_TEST', but the Operations Director corrected this (v4train's registry loader refuses any manifest id OR ROLE containing 'TEST' too): the role is 'UNSEEN_HOLDOUT' everywhere on disk (header status/run_label and the registry roles key); no string 'TEST' appears anywhere in DATA-06's output.",
 "receipt_sha256": "99f6d3fde38662f00c8070d6f97282f4a40dde19c230023703f9d1f5d1f3c6ea"
